{"id": 55, "ts": 1780423969.0522676, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 3, "agent": "emily_brooks", "message": "I appreciate Sarah\u2019s clarification that Candidate\u202fB has been observed as uncooperative and grumpy, which raises serious doubts about his crew\u2011cooperation and professional communication\u2014both non\u2011negotiable for long\u2011haul operations. While B\u2019s conscientiousness and stress handling are strong, the lack of constructive teamwork outweighs those benefits in a safety\u2011critical cockpit.\nComparing that to Candidate\u202fD, we have evidence that D \u201ctakes responsibility seriously,\u201d \u201csolves problems extremely well,\u201d \u201ccan concentrate very well,\u201d and \u201cresponds to unexpected events adequately.\u201d These traits map directly to operational reliability, decision quality, attention accuracy, and responsibility\u2014core criteria for our long\u2011distance pilot role. Although D is described as moody and a loner, those concerns are less prohibitive than outright uncooperativeness, and they can be mitigated through crew\u2011resource\u2011management training.\nGiven the current evidence, I now recommend Candidate\u202fD as the strongest overall fit."}
