{"id": 60, "ts": 1780423994.7262218, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 4, "agent": "sarah_mitchell", "message": "I\u2019d like to build on the earlier points about reliability and crew dynamics. Candidate\u202fC is the only one we know to be\u202f100\u202f% reliable\u202fand also creates a positive atmosphere with his crew, which directly supports both operational reliability and crew cooperation\u2014key for long\u2011distance flights. Moreover, he can make correct decisions quickly, addressing the decision\u2011quality and stress\u2011resilience criteria.\nThe concerns you\u2019ve heard\u2014difficulty communicating ideas, an egocentric style, and limited willingness for further education\u2014are real, but they are offset by his proven reliability and the fact that he already fosters a good cockpit environment. In contrast, Candidate\u202fA shows leadership but is unorganized; Candidate\u202fB handles stress but can be uncooperative; Candidate\u202fD is responsible yet is regarded as arrogant with weak leadership. Given the balance of strengths and the critical importance of reliability and crew harmony, I remain convinced that Candidate\u202fC is the best overall fit."}
